.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_SIGNATURE-RSA 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_SIGNATURE-RSA
.Nd The EVP_PKEY RSA signature implementation
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Support for computing RSA signatures.
See
.Xr EVP_PKEY-RSA 7
for information related to RSA keys.
.Ss Algorithm Names
In this list, names are grouped together to signify that they are the
same algorithm having multiple names.
This also includes the OID in canonical decimal form (which means that
they are possible to fetch if the caller has a mere OID which came out
in this form after a call to
.Xr OBJ_obj2txt 3 Ns ).
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqRSA", \(dqrsaEncryption", \(dq1.2.840.113549.1.1.1"
The base signature algorithm, supported explicitly fetched with
.Xr EVP_PKEY_sign_init_ex2 3 ,
and implicitly fetched (through
.Xr EVP_PKEY-RSA 7 )
with
.Xr EVP_DigestSignInit 3
and
.Xr EVP_DigestVerifyInit 3 .
.Pp
It can't be used with
.Xr EVP_PKEY_sign_message_init 3
.It \(dqRSA-RIPEMD160", \(dqripemd160WithRSA", \(dq1.3.36.3.3.1.2"
.It \(dqRSA-SHA2-256", \(dqRSA-SHA256", \(dqsha256WithRSAEncryption", \(dq1.2.840.113549.1.1.11"
.It \(dqRSA-SHA2-384", \(dqRSA-SHA384", \(dqsha384WithRSAEncryption", \(dq1.2.840.113549.1.1.12"
.It \(dqRSA-SHA2-512", \(dqRSA-SHA512", \(dqsha512WithRSAEncryption", \(dq1.2.840.113549.1.1.13"
.It \(dqRSA-SHA2-224", \(dqRSA-SHA224", \(dqsha224WithRSAEncryption", \(dq1.2.840.113549.1.1.14"
.It \(dqRSA-SHA2-512/224", \(dqRSA-SHA512-224", \(dqsha512-224WithRSAEncryption", \(dq1.2.840.113549.1.1.15"
.It \(dqRSA-SHA2-512/256", \(dqRSA-SHA512-256", \(dqsha512-256WithRSAEncryption", \(dq1.2.840.113549.1.1.16"
.It \(dqRSA-SHA3-224", \(dqid-rsassa-pkcs1-v1_5-with-sha3-224", \(dq2.16.840.1.101.3.4.3.13"
.It \(dqRSA-SHA3-256", \(dqid-rsassa-pkcs1-v1_5-with-sha3-256", \(dq2.16.840.1.101.3.4.3.14"
.It \(dqRSA-SHA3-384", \(dqid-rsassa-pkcs1-v1_5-with-sha3-384", \(dq2.16.840.1.101.3.4.3.15"
.It \(dqRSA-SHA3-512", \(dqid-rsassa-pkcs1-v1_5-with-sha3-512", \(dq2.16.840.1.101.3.4.3.16"
.It \(dqRSA-SM3", \(dqsm3WithRSAEncryption", \(dq1.2.156.10197.1.504"
PKCS#1 v1.5 RSA signature schemes with diverse message digest
algorithms.
They are all supported explicitly fetched with
.Xr EVP_PKEY_sign_init_ex2 3
and
.Xr EVP_PKEY_sign_message_init 3 .
They are all pre-set to use the pad mode "pkcs1". This cannot be
changed.
.El
.Ss Signature Parameters
The following signature parameters can be set using
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_set_params 3 .
This may be called after
.Xr EVP_PKEY_sign_init 3
or
.Xr EVP_PKEY_verify_init 3 ,
and before calling
.Xr EVP_PKEY_sign 3
or
.Xr EVP_PKEY_verify 3 .
They may also be set using
.Xr EVP_PKEY_sign_init_ex 3
or
.Xr EVP_PKEY_verify_init_ex 3 .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqdigest" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_DIGEST Ns ) <UTF8 string>
.It \(dqproperties" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_PROPERTIES Ns ) <UTF8 string>
These are not supported with the RSA signature schemes that already
include a message digest algorithm, See
.Sx Algorithm Names
above.
.Pp
These common parameters are described in
.Xr provider-signature 7 .
.It \(dqpad-mode" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_PAD_MODE Ns ) <UTF8 string>
The type of padding to be used.
Its value can be one of the following:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqnone" ( Ns Sy OSSL_PKEY_RSA_PAD_MODE_NONE )
.It \(dqpkcs1" ( Ns Sy OSSL_PKEY_RSA_PAD_MODE_PKCSV15 )
.It \(dqx931" ( Ns Sy OSSL_PKEY_RSA_PAD_MODE_X931 )
This padding mode is no longer supported by the FIPS provider for
signature generation, but may be used for signature verification for
legacy use cases.
(This is a FIPS 140-3 requirement)
.It \(dqpss" ( Ns Sy OSSL_PKEY_RSA_PAD_MODE_PSS )
.El
.It \(dqmgf1-digest" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_MGF1_DIGEST Ns ) <UTF8 string>
The digest algorithm name to use for the maskGenAlgorithm used by "pss"
mode.
.It \(dqmgf1-properties" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_MGF1_PROPERTIES Ns ) <UTF8 string>
Sets the name of the property query associated with the "mgf1-digest"
algorithm.
NULL is used if this optional value is not set.
.It \(dqsaltlen" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_PSS_SALTLEN Ns ) <integer> or <UTF8 string>
The "pss" mode minimum salt length.
The value can either be an integer, a string value representing a number
or one of the following string values:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqdigest" ( Ns Sy OSSL_PKEY_RSA_PSS_SALT_LEN_DIGEST )
Use the same length as the digest size.
.It \(dqmax" ( Ns Sy OSSL_PKEY_RSA_PSS_SALT_LEN_MAX )
Use the maximum salt length.
.It \(dqauto" ( Ns Sy OSSL_PKEY_RSA_PSS_SALT_LEN_AUTO )
Auto detect the salt length.
.It \(dqauto-digestmax" ( Ns Sy OSSL_PKEY_RSA_PSS_SALT_LEN_AUTO_DIGEST_MAX )
Auto detect the salt length when verifying.
Maximize the salt length up to the digest size when signing to comply
with FIPS 186-4 section 5.5.
.El
.El
.Pp
The OpenSSL FIPS provider also supports the following parameters:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqkey-check" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_FIPS_KEY_CHECK Ns ) <integer>
.It \(dqdigest-check" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_FIPS_DIGEST_CHECK Ns ) <integer>
.It \(dqsign-x931-pad-check" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_FIPS_SIGN_X931_PAD_CHECK Ns ) <integer>
These parameters are described in
.Xr provider-signature 7 .
.It \(dqrsa-pss-saltlen-check" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_FIPS_RSA_PSS_SALTLEN_CHECK Ns ) <integer>
The default value of 1 causes an error during signature generation or
verification if salt length
.Pf ( Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_PSS_SALTLEN )
is not between zero and the output block size of the digest function
(inclusive).
Setting this to zero will ignore the error and set the approved
"fips-indicator" to 0. This option breaks FIPS compliance if it causes
the approved "fips-indicator" to return 0.
.El
.Pp
The following signature parameters can be retrieved using
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_get_params 3 .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqalgorithm-id" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_ALGORITHM_ID Ns ) <octet string>
.It \(dqfips-indicator" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_FIPS_APPROVED_INDICATOR Ns ) <integer>
.It \(dqverify-message" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_FIPS_VERIFY_MESSAGE No <integer>
These common parameter are described in
.Xr provider-signature 7 .
.It \(dqdigest" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_DIGEST Ns ) <UTF8 string>
.It \(dqpad-mode" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_PAD_MODE Ns ) <UTF8 string>
.It \(dqmgf1-digest" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_MGF1_DIGEST Ns ) <UTF8 string>
.It \(dqsaltlen" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_PSS_SALTLEN Ns ) <integer> or <UTF8 string>
These parameters are as described above.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_set_params 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_sign 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_verify 3 ,
.Xr provider-signature 7 ,
